From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:39:54 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] feat(desktop): the v4 models get their own research
 grid

The Overview's research panel only held results for the 2026-09-12 model set
(41ded2cdd5c2ba3f), so the v4 edition showed another model's numbers. It now
carries one grid per model set and shows the grid of the models the running
edition ships.

- research-data.ts: RESEARCH_PROFILES_V4 for artifact 53b6f14244c2e633 -
  baseline, +SLAC 10 s and +SLAC 600 ms under the published, strict and
  reviewed labels. Generated from ev_charger_ai
  results/research_grid_v4.json (benchmark/research_grid_from_cache.py): the
  v4 first-alert records rescored per label profile, with the cached SLAC
  fire times projected onto them - no replay. The same method reproduces all
  180 shipped 41ded2cd numbers exactly; v4 strict.baseline equals the v4
  leaderboard to full precision; an independent re-implementation matched 15
  of 15 cells. RESEARCH_GRIDS lists both sets with their provenance.
- selectResearchGrid() picks the grid by the sidecar's artifact id, else by
  an exact baseline-arm leaderboard match; disagreement falls back to the
  first grid and says "unknown".
- ISO 15118-2 was never replayed for v4: its tab is disabled with "not
  measured (needs a replay)". Projected arms say so, and for v4 AI Agent's
  recall and false-alarm rate are marked as lower bounds (its evidence board
  is not replayed; 0.0-0.2 points low on 41ded2cd).
- On the published labels the v4 grid warns that those labels count 369
  sessions it was trained to flag (NO_POWER_DELIVERED 360, SLAC 9) as clean -
  measured: excluding them makes every published false-alarm rate equal the
  strict one, alert for alert.

Tests: 16 files / 294 pass; tsc adds no error anywhere.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
